Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.58,0:02:05.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Hello, Azalar.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.34,0:02:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Shedar.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.90,0:02:11.18,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been a long time \Nsince you last visited me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.14,0:02:13.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm glad to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.78,0:02:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Come, step inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.14,0:02:19.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I have always been waiting for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.44,0:02:22.65,Default,,0,0,0,,To be honest,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.12,0:02:24.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I was afraid of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.60,0:02:28.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I worried that someday \Nyou might burn Mother,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.60,0:02:30.71,Default,,0,0,0,,or pass your sickness on to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.70,0:02:31.80,Default,,0,0,0,,That was my concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.04,0:02:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,The Queen herself is the cause of my illness.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.00,0:02:42.39,Default,,0,0,0,,If she hadn't used the magic \Nof the Dofus so excessively,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.08,0:02:44.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't have ended up like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.72,0:02:47.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Besides, I never would have
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.60,0:02:50.32,Default,,0,0,0,,become this submissive either.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.05,0:02:58.27,Default,,0,0,0,,All of your mother's success is \Nentirely thanks to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.09,0:03:01.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Even the Queen cannot deny that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.76,0:03:05.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did you come here?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.96,0:03:07.53,Default,,0,0,0,,You must have a reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.08,0:03:08.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Azalar,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.28,0:03:11.29,Default,,0,0,0,,you went to Breshka, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.96,0:03:13.09,Default,,0,0,0,,What about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:13.80,0:03:16.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you find Canel's son?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.88,0:03:17.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.66,0:03:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.82,0:03:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,you...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.90,0:03:24.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't kill him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.86,0:03:27.70,Default,,0,0,0,,I was thwarted by General Marmiton and Joris.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.94,0:03:35.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Those two concocted a scheme \Nto hide Canel's son for over 15 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.86,0:03:38.80,Default,,0,0,0,,So my dream was real after all?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.86,0:03:40.61,Default,,0,0,0,,That was no simple dream.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.63,0:03:43.74,Default,,0,0,0,,My brother, Dardondakal,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.74,0:03:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,showed that to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.83,0:03:46.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Dakal?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.43,0:03:50.09,Default,,0,0,0,,He appears deep within people's consciousness
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.43,0:03:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,and weaves a few truths into a web of lies.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.07,0:03:56.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Then, those who awaken
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.03,0:04:00.21,Default,,0,0,0,,that they received a divine revelation.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.58,0:04:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't be deceived.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.90,0:04:11.10,Default,,0,0,0,,The only thing that matters \Nis your mother's words.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.58,0:04:12.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.74,0:04:15.86,Default,,0,0,0,,But Canel's son is also my cousin.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.70,0:04:19.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead of killing him, \Ncan't we just lock him in a dungeon?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.83,0:04:22.21,Default,,0,0,0,,That would only leave seeds of trouble for the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.51,0:04:24.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Besides, just as you said,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.11,0:04:27.37,Default,,0,0,0,,do you really think keeping him chained in a cell for life
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.91,0:04:30.61,Default,,0,0,0,,would actually be doing him a favor?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.59,0:04:32.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.39,0:04:34.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Now go.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.31,0:04:38.34,Default,,0,0,0,,To avoid displeasing your mother,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.67,0:04:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I must fulfill my duty.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.73,0:04:53.23,Default,,0,0,0,,To rule a kingdom,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.89,0:04:56.87,Default,,0,0,0,,one is sometimes forced to make difficult decisions.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.57,0:05:00.15,Default,,0,0,0,,You too must understand that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.56,0:05:02.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.08,0:05:03.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.54,0:05:31.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Show yourself, Shifo.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.31,0:05:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Father, hello. \NIt's an honor to see you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.03,0:05:46.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you to stay in your true form \Nwhenever you speak to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.35,0:05:49.18,Default,,0,0,0,,I am sorry, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.46,0:05:56.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.02,0:05:59.15,Default,,0,0,0,,There is something I wish to entrust to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.79,0:06:02.55,Default,,0,0,0,,This will be a good chance for you to travel the outside world.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.22,0:06:04.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that true, Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.26,0:06:08.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I need your keen nose.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.20,0:06:15.51,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the scent of a boy's blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.20,0:06:18.47,Default,,0,0,0,,It smells very similar to the Queen and the Prince.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.20,0:06:22.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Track him down and kill him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.60,0:06:27.65,Default,,0,0,0,,If you succeed, I shall grant you an audience with the Queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.00,0:06:30.30,Default,,0,0,0,,She will surely reward you handsomely.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.64,0:06:31.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The Queen...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.24,0:06:33.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Understood, Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.26,0:06:47.46,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been so long since I breathed fresh air.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.82,0:07:32.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Smell this.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.67,0:07:39.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this licorice tea?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.87,0:07:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, it's Bakara's favorite tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.99,0:07:43.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Bakara?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.35,0:07:47.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Khan's wife. \NOur mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.59,0:07:58.37,Default,,0,0,0,,My, how impressive!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.99,0:08:02.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Your friend's cooking was absolutely delicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.87,0:08:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you shouldn't stop at omelets! \NYou should try his pies, stews, and gratins too!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.95,0:08:09.74,Default,,0,0,0,,They are unbelievably tasty!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.07,0:08:13.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah! I'm ready to eat anytime!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.99,0:08:14.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\b1}*{\i1}Burp{\i0}*{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.39,0:08:18.12,Default,,0,0,0,,He really takes after his father, doesn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.43,0:08:20.72,Default,,0,0,0,,That is proof of his true bloodline!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.47,0:08:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Gobbowl players have to be careful \Nnot to trap air in their stomachs, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.71,0:08:30.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I see. \NTruly a real pro.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.23,0:08:33.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\b1}Meow{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.35,0:08:38.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, what are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.95,0:08:45.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't see Moo go through the portal.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.45,0:08:48.25,Default,,0,0,0,,How on earth did you find us?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.94,0:08:52.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Moo?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.22,0:08:55.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this little one your cat?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.90,0:08:56.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.30,0:09:00.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama used to tell me that Moo had been taking care of me ever since I was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.24,0:09:02.18,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what mama said.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.97,0:09:07.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Ever since I was born, Moo kept picking on me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.16,0:09:10.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, we can't choose our family, can we?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.05,0:09:16.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Speaking of family. Master Joris, \Nplease tell us your story.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.21,0:09:18.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright then.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.32,0:09:25.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know anything about Queen Zabel?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.80,0:09:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Queen Zabel rules over Sufokia, Amakna, and Bonta.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.72,0:09:36.84,Default,,0,0,0,,She is one of the most powerful rulers in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.03,0:09:43.70,Default,,0,0,0,,She is called the Queen of Darkness because she bound herself to the black dragon, Azalar.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.47,0:09:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,His true name is Grozagran Azaral.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.59,0:09:49.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean the monster that attacked us, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.19,0:09:50.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.71,0:09:56.30,Default,,0,0,0,,The only reason you weren't killed was because he was weakened by sickness.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.09,0:09:59.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Azalar mind is captive to Zabel.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.17,0:10:05.54,Default,,0,0,0,,And Zabel has only one ambition: to rule over every realm.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.01,0:10:09.18,Default,,0,0,0,,What does any of this have to do with me?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.31,0:10:14.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Your father's name was Canel Sheran Sharm.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.79,0:10:20.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Canel was the King of Bonta and \None of the greatest heroes in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.07,0:10:24.33,Default,,0,0,0,,And Zabel was Canel's younger sister.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.04,0:10:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Twenty-six years ago, two witches, the Grimalkin sisters, \Nappeared in the Kingdom of Bonta.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.72,0:10:37.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Those two witches brought about countless tragedies,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.10,0:10:44.85,Default,,0,0,0,,And after endless destruction and slaughter, \Nthe Grimalkin sisters usurped the throne of Bonta.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.03,0:10:50.81,Default,,0,0,0,,We lent our strength to Canel and Zabel \Nto stand against the Grimalkin sisters together.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.68,0:10:58.84,Default,,0,0,0,,The two witches possessed the Crimson Dofus and the Turquoise Dofus, yielding immense magical power.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.96,0:11:04.80,Default,,0,0,0,,To defeat them, Zabel and Canel also \Nneeded to obtain Dofus of their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.48,0:11:11.44,Default,,0,0,0,,The war was long, painful, and bloody, but in the end, the sisters were defeated.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.52,0:11:18.76,Default,,0,0,0,,The heroes were hailed by the people, and chosen as the King of Bonta and the Queen of Amakna.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.56,0:11:22.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Peace returned to both kingdoms for over ten years.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.56,0:11:27.08,Default,,0,0,0,,However, the way they used their Dofus was completely different.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.15,0:11:33.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Canel realized that channeling the power of a Dofus was a double-edged sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.15,0:11:39.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Meanwhile, Zabel, who possessed the Ebony Dofus, used its magic at every opportunity,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.30,0:11:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,From accelerating crop growth to forging magical weaponry.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.62,0:11:51.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Between Zabel and Azalar, \Nan unbreakable bond gradually began to form.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.26,0:11:56.18,Default,,0,0,0,,And eventually, the Queen and the Dragon became as one.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.90,0:12:05.02,Default,,0,0,0,,As Zabel's ambitions grew stronger, she began plotting to take over her brother's kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.22,0:12:19.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Zabel, my little sister, there must be another way!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.19,0:12:25.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us walk along the ramparts together, just like when we were children, and find a solution!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.12,0:12:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Let us remember who we truly are!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.30,0:12:37.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Canel, dwelling on memories is pointless. \NI don't even know what I've become anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.65,0:12:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I should have listened to you years ago, but I failed to do so!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.33,0:12:48.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Zabel, please, you can still turn back!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.90,0:12:53.64,Default,,0,0,0,,No need to hold back.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.23,0:13:09.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, having fun, are we?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.73,0:13:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Opportunities to unleash a Dofus's power \Ndon't come often, after all! It's pure bliss!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.22,0:13:20.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Around that same time, The Queen, Anette went into labor.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.93,0:13:25.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Welsh, your mother was always so kind.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.00,0:13:29.21,Default,,0,0,0,,She possessed a power unique to the Belafons.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.09,0:13:34.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Through a powerful spell, your parents' hearts were deeply connected.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.61,0:13:38.81,Default,,0,0,0,,They shared both their thoughts and their pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.08,0:13:47.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Their bond was extraordinary. so deep that if one died, \Nthe other would perish instantly as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.23,0:13:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Welsh, Canel was not fighting for himself alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.07,0:14:04.31,Default,,0,0,0,,The lives of his wife and unborn child were riding on his hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.50,0:14:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My love!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.20,0:14:08.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My love, the baby is coming!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.14,0:14:13.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I see. Don't worry. \NI won't fall so easily!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.52,0:14:16.72,Default,,0,0,0,,My, getting tired already?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.19,0:14:21.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Anette's labor has begun! \NYou're about to become an aunt!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.99,0:14:25.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Zabel! Let's end this conflict now!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.50,0:14:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't interfere! I came here to take your life, Canel!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.60,0:14:36.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't stop until you are dead!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.65,0:14:39.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Almost there Canel...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.21,0:14:46.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can feel everything you're experiencing, Anette.\NSo, is this the suffering of darkness?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.78,0:14:47.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yes, Canel!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.96,0:14:49.80,Default,,0,0,0,,My queen, just a little more!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.28,0:14:52.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anette, I am right here with you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.74,0:15:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He looks just like Canel! \NA healthy baby boy!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.71,0:15:14.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As soon as this battle is over, \NI will come see you immediately.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.75,0:15:18.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Be careful, Canel. \NZabel is serious!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:18.83,0:15:21.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She's my sister. \NSurely she doesn't intend to kill me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.52,0:15:30.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We've lived together all our lives, after all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.04,0:16:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the end, Zabel! \NGet up, and greet your nephew. My son!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.48,0:16:08.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Haven't you been listening to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.86,0:16:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,You fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.37,0:16:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,CANEL!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.65,0:16:26.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't look at me like that. \NI warned you countless times!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.65,0:16:27.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Zabel...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.16,0:16:44.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Joris, run with this child! \NHide him, and protect him!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.50,0:16:47.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Anette!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.83,0:16:58.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Even like this, you can still smile?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.11,0:17:03.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You will regret your actions for the rest of your life!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.51,0:17:09.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I am fully prepared for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.95,0:17:19.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Anette...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.84,0:17:34.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.44,0:18:10.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fs22\b1\3c&HAFAFAF&\2c&HFFFFFF&\c&HFFFFFF&\pos(98.133,251.733)}Episode 3 Licorice Tea
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.96,0:18:10.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\fnArial\fs14\pos(195.2,285.156)}After that, I entrusted you to General Marmiton.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.16,0:18:14.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I intended to wait a few more years \Nbefore coming to get you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.23,0:18:20.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps I should have told you everything much sooner.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.27,0:18:25.53,Default,,0,0,0,,However, we concealed your \Ntrue identity solely to protect you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.31,0:18:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Zabel has spies everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.91,0:18:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The fewer people who knew the secret, \Nthe less likely you would be in danger. 
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.08,0:18:39.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That's how it was supposed to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.48,0:18:44.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet somehow, Zabel found out about your existence.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:45.84,0:18:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone in your family has clear blue eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.56,0:18:53.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Someone in Breshka might have noticed \Nand reported it to the Dark Queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.40,0:18:58.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Only a handful of us knew this secret.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.08,0:19:03.72,Default,,0,0,0,,If there were a traitor among us, \Nthey would have betrayed us long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.07,0:19:09.73,Default,,0,0,0,,What am I supposed to do now? \NAre you telling me to fight the Dark Queen?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.75,0:19:14.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if I could beat Jabelle with a frying pan and a fork.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.18,0:19:19.46,Default,,0,0,0,,A cook from Breshka like me could never become king!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.26,0:19:25.74,Default,,0,0,0,,You're trying to send a kid like me into a fight I can't win!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.18,0:19:26.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Welsh...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.82,0:19:30.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, what about it? \NAnswer me, Master Joris!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.10,0:19:36.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Why did my parents die even though \Nyou were right by their side?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.22,0:19:50.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Bechamel, what are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.90,0:19:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Cheer up, Welsh! \NFinding out you're actually a prince isn't so bad, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.02,0:19:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you seriously saying that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.24,0:20:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,If that's the case, \Nwhy don't you go on this adventure instead of me, Becha?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.81,0:20:06.19,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you when we were little that I was an orphan, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.17,0:20:12.51,Default,,0,0,0,,When the Dark Queen attacked Bonta, \Nmy village was right in their path.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.05,0:20:17.47,Default,,0,0,0,,They took away all the food and \Nall the men who could fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.62,0:20:22.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I was dragged off by bandits too, \Nbut I managed to escape when they weren't looking.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.78,0:20:27.35,Default,,0,0,0,,The other kids with me weren't as lucky as I was...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.82,0:20:28.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Becha...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.94,0:20:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Welsh, if you go on an adventure, \NI'm coming with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.06,0:20:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, aren't you going to answer me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.98,0:20:46.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Welsh!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.99,0:21:04.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Who goes there? \NAre we on the right path, Shifo?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.63,0:21:09.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Calm down, I'm no enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.98,0:21:14.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Prince Shedar... \NIt's a pleasure to meet you for the first time.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.90,0:21:18.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Shifo, why are you obeying Azalar's every command?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.38,0:21:25.39,Default,,0,0,0,,My father gives orders, and I obey. \NAzalar is my father and my master, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.14,0:21:26.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.49,0:21:29.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Then feel free to continue your pursuit.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.37,0:21:32.48,Default,,0,0,0,,That is my father's order.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.93,0:21:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Even without you telling me-
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.46,0:21:39.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I am the Prince of Bonta. \NMy orders take precedence over Azalar's.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.56,0:21:47.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry, I just want to ensure Canel's son \Nposes no threat to my mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.36,0:21:54.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Understood, my Prince. \NHowever, I won't slow down our pace. \NCan you keep up?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.94,0:21:59.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I've already been following behind you \Nfor a hundred leagues!
